# CardDemo Frontend — local environment variable template.
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` (which the root .gitignore ignores and which
# must NEVER be committed), then adjust the values for your environment.
#
# This template holds ONLY non-sensitive, public configuration. Every variable
# whose name begins with NEXT_PUBLIC_ is inlined into the client JavaScript
# bundle at `next build` time and is therefore publicly visible in the browser.
# NEVER put secrets (API keys, database credentials, JWT signing keys,
# passwords) in a NEXT_PUBLIC_ variable. Server-only secrets belong in the
# backend's own configuration (see backend/.env.example), never here.
# (Ochs Rule #3 — no hardcoded secrets; use environment variables instead.)

# API configuration
#
# Base URL / origin of the FastAPI backend. The backend listens on port 8000.
#
# The backend mounts all of its REST routers under the `/api/v1` prefix
# (see backend/.env.example -> API_V1_PREFIX=/api/v1). The axios client in
# `src/lib/apiClient.ts` builds its baseURL by appending that prefix as
# `${NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL}/api/v1`, so an endpoint such as `POST /auth/login`
# resolves to `http://localhost:8000/api/v1/auth/login`. For that reason the
# value below is the backend ORIGIN only — do NOT append the `/api/v1` suffix.
#
# Under docker-compose, keep this as the host-mapped origin
# `http://localhost:8000` rather than the compose service name
# `http://backend:8000`: NEXT_PUBLIC_ values run in the browser, which reaches
# the backend on the host-published port, not on the compose-internal network.
#
# Build-time note: because NEXT_PUBLIC_ values are inlined at build time, this
# variable must be present when `next build` runs (locally and in CI), not only
# at runtime.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:8000

# Optional, non-sensitive label for the running environment (informational
# only; safe to expose). Uncomment and adjust if your code chooses to read it.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ENV=development
